# Cost-Aware Model Routing (Agent Requested)

Premise: **Cursor Pro = $20/month included.** Frontier models (Claude/GPT) burn this budget fast.

> Default to Cursor-native (cheap). Use frontier only when truly needed, sparingly. When budget runs low, fall back to Cursor-native entirely.

## Tiers (paperthin `modelchk` = vendor-neutral three-step)

Set two dials before starting: **capability tier** + **reasoning effort** (glance → moderate → deep → exhaustive). Don't reflexively max the effort — that burns tokens.

| Tier | When | Cursor model | Cost |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **fast** | Trivial edits, formatting, repetition, mechanical work | Composer / Auto | included |
| **standard** | Most implementation, scaffolding, MVP first version | Grok / Composer / Auto | included~low |
| **frontier** | High-risk logic (auth/payment/security), tricky debugging, key design review | Claude / GPT | **API-metered (expensive)** |

## Budget guard (★ core)

- Frontier is **escalation-only**, never the default. Raise to it only when `modelchk` says the task truly needs it.
- Keep frontier to **short plan/review segments**; run long build loops on standard.
- When budget/tokens run low → **degrade**: everything to Cursor-native (Composer/Auto/Grok); no frontier calls.
- Start cheap when unsure; escalate one step only if the result falls short.
